      <memberdef kind="variable" id="group__horiz__interp__spherical__mod_1gabf353472de82554fcbc7ffdb9ca24a8d" prot="private" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>character(len=32)</type>
        <definition>character(len=32) search_method</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>search_method</name>
        <initializer>= &quot;radial_search&quot;</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Namelist variable to indicate the searching method to find the nearest neighbor points. Its value can be &quot;radial_search&quot; and &quot;full_search&quot;, with default value &quot;radial_search&quot;. when search_method is &quot;radial_search&quot;, the search may be not quite accurate for some cases. Normally the search will be ok if you chose suitable max_dist. When search_method is &quot;full_search&quot;, it will be always accurate, but will be slower comparing to &quot;radial_search&quot;. Normally these two search algorithm will produce same results other than order of operation. &quot;radial_search&quot; are recommended to use. The purpose to add &quot;full_search&quot; is in case you think you interpolation results is not right, you have other option to verify. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
